## 4. Hook Wrappers

Each app exposes a `useAuth()` hook that selects individual properties from the auth store. This provides a clean API for components and maintains backward compatibility with the previous `useState`-based `useAuth()` hook.

**Pattern:**
```typescript
// hooks/useAuth.ts
"use client";
import { useAuthStore } from "@/store/authStore";

export function useAuth() {
  const user = useAuthStore((state) => state.user);
  const isAuthenticated = useAuthStore((state) => state.isAuthenticated);
  const login = useAuthStore((state) => state.login);
  const logout = useAuthStore((state) => state.logout);
  // ...
  return { user, isAuthenticated, login, logout };
}
```

**Why individual selectors instead of a single `useAuthStore()` call?**
Zustand re-renders components only when the selected slice of state changes. Selecting individual properties prevents unnecessary re-renders. For example, a component that only reads `isAuthenticated` will not re-render when `isLoading` changes.

The CRM frontend also provides a backward-compatible `useToast()` hook exported from `Toast.tsx`:
```typescript
// components/ui/Toast.tsx
export function useToast() {
  const toasts = useUiStore((state) => state.toasts);
  const addToast = useUiStore((state) => state.addToast);
  // ...
  return { messages: toasts, addToast, dismissToast, success, error, info };
}
```

